8. Definitions

"Access" to a particular form of code or content means (a) the substantial
and timely opportunity to obtain a copy of such code or content; (b) any
necessary and corresponding information about such code or content,
including any necessary Cryptographic Keys; and (c) such information as is
necessary to enable independent use of such code or content.

"Cryptographic Keys" means any encryption keys, decryption keys,
authentication keys, signing keys, or any combination thereof used to
protect, secure, or authenticate the Work, User Data, Personal Data, or
any communications, transactions, or operations involving the Work.

"Derivative Work" means a work that is based upon, derived from, or
incorporates the Work, in whole or in part, in any form, and includes,
without limitation, all modifications, improvements, adaptations, or
enhancements of the Work.

"License" has the meaning given in Section 1.

"Licensed Patents" means patent claims licensable by a Licensor that are
necessarily infringed by the Work alone or by combinations of the Work
with other works.

"Licensor" means the party or parties offering the License, including any
party that subsequently distributes a Derivative Work under the License.

"Permission" means any consent, authorization, or license granted by
Licensor under this License.

"Personal Data" means any information relating to an identified or
identifiable natural person, where an identifiable natural person is one
who can be identified, directly or indirectly, by reference to an
identifier such as a name, an identification number, location data, an
online identifier, or to one or more factors specific to that natural
person.

"Recipient" means any party that has received a License under this
License.

"Source Code" means the form of a work preferred for making modifications,
including any comments, configuration files, scripts used to control
compilation and installation of an executable, or other equivalent
information.

"Source Code Form" means the Source Code of the Work or any Derivative
Work.

"User" means a party that has the right under this License or another
applicable agreement to operate the Work on a device or system controlled
by the User, whether the Work is run locally or remotely (such as over a
network).

"User Data" means any data that is an input to or an output from the Work,
where the presence of the data is necessary for substantive
functionality to be provided by the Work to the User, where the User has
an existing ownership interest in such data (whether by virtue of being
the source of the data or having an enforceable contractual or other
legal right concerning such data), where such data includes Personal Data
of the User, or where such data is otherwise specifically identified by
the Recipient or the Licensor as User Data.

"Work" means the software made available under this License, including the
Source Code and any binaries or other executable forms thereof.
